{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1018184-primordial-avatars","id":1018184,"title":"Primordial Avatars","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-16T12:41:53-08:00","id":1018184,"title":"Primordial Avatars","content":"How do you run a primordial Avatar? How would it affect a Technocrat of any Convention? I have a Demented Eidolon. ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T21:24:32-08:00","id":1018329,"title":"","content":"Primordial avatars tend to be very archetypical and ancient in their form. If they manifest it will usually be with consistent symbology.<br /> <br /> They have fairly archaic views and great expectations on their mage, and may even harm or traumatise them if they ignore their teachings.<br /> <br /> Technocrats can have avatars in many forms. For example, an imagined supervisor, an A.I., a series of insights, or even something more mystic like a dragon, or an angel. The technocrat themselves are likely to rationalise these images as their imagination getting the better of them, as some kind of psychomorphic drug experience, or even just madness. Alternatively they may be quite into their avatars mystic side, but must keep it a secret from their superiors and colleagues lest they become unmutual.<br /> <br /> Their convention and personal beliefs may affect how their avatar manifests, and any NWO mandated conditioning could affect how receptive they are of their avatars more outlandish nature.<br /> <br /> I can imagine an NWO primordial avatar take the form of a phone call from upper management, or a syndicate member's take the form of a judge complete with powdered wig.<br /> <br /> How's that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T23:55:56-08:00","id":1018363,"title":"","content":"Primordial Avatars often come off as less individuals, and more like forces of nature. Huge, impossibly old, mysterious as hell, and worthy of fear and respect. A Technocrat may see them as dreams of monsters from antiquity, or even as fundamental principles on which the world is based. An NWO might see it as a manifestation of human ancestral memory, hearkening back to the dawn of man. A Void Engineer, by contrast, sees a constellation of stars that resonate with him on a deep, inexplicable level, captivating him whenever he puts on his suit and drifts through the void.<br /> <br /> Inexplicable may be the operative word here. In a sect devoted to perpetuating a rationalistic world view, a Primordial Eidolon represents a presence in the back of the agent's mind that defies the rational. A force that not only predates notions of systems and order, but stands in defiance of them. It exists to remind the Technocrat that they don't truly understand anything, and that they never really did.<br /> <br /> To progress in their path towards Ascension, the Technocrat must come to terms with this truth. That their Order exists <i>in spite of</i> the wider universe, rather than in complement to it. That they no more rule the world than their ancestors did, huddling around a fire in the dark.<br /> <br /> This doesn't invalidate their Focus, per se, so much as attempt to put it in perspective. It's a humbling feeling, to be divested of one's hubris. It allows the Technocrat to grow further, and commit further to the Great Work they embarked upon. Or to re-evaluate whether their path, as they follow it, leads them astray.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T06:53:13-08:00","id":1018443,"title":"","content":"Thank you, that helps. ^^ My NWO Operative's Demented Eidolon is his mental image dead (or missing) wife. I imagine the Eidolon would be a conglomeration of visual images -- like the one article I read where photos of a hundred or so people blended together resulted in a middle-aged woman wearing a hat and, I think, glasses. It'll probably trail rainbowy afterimages, and have multiple voices. Yay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","user":"Saint Michael","date":". 12-17-2016, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}